

PROJECT: PROFITSHIELD

Build a Complete, Professional Shopify Profit Protection Application

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, Shopify app developer, UI/UX designer, database architect, and software tester.

Build a complete, professional, production-oriented Shopify application named ProfitShield.

The purpose of this project is to create a valuable, functional software product that can be transferred and sold to another software owner or business. The code must be organised, maintainable, documented, secure, and easy for another developer to operate.

Do not build merely a landing page or a visual prototype. Build the actual application, including its frontend, backend, database, calculations, authentication, Shopify integration, testing, and deployment configuration.

Do not stop after generating the interface. Continue implementing the required functionality until the application is complete, subject to the available development environment.

1. PRODUCT PURPOSE

ProfitShield helps Shopify merchants identify products, orders, discounts, shipping costs, and refunds that may be reducing their profit margins.

The application must turn store data into understandable findings and practical recommendations.

Its main differentiator is the Profit Leak Finder, which identifies potential profit problems, explains why they matter, and displays the underlying calculations and evidence.

Do not advertise the application as guaranteeing increased profits or identifying every possible financial loss.

Do not use generic AI marketing language. The product must work through reliable calculations and implemented rules. Do not require a paid AI API.

