9. PROFIT CALCULATION ENGINE

Build the calculation engine as separate, tested JavaScript functions.

Where the required fields are available, calculate:

Net sales:
	•	Product sales after applicable discounts and adjustments.
	•	Use a clearly documented definition and avoid subtracting discounts twice.

Estimated gross profit:
	•	Applicable net sales minus the corresponding cost of goods sold.

Estimated gross margin:
	•	Estimated gross profit divided by applicable net sales, multiplied by 100.

Discount impact:
	•	Compare the estimated profit before a discount with the estimated profit after the discount, keeping other assumptions consistent.

Shipping impact:
	•	Compare shipping revenue, where available, with actual shipping expenses.
	•	Do not assume shipping revenue and shipping expense are the same.

Refund impact:
	•	Use actual refund information and available cost information.
	•	Document how returned inventory and restocking are treated.
	•	Do not assume every refunded product returns to sellable inventory.

Estimated contribution after available expenses:
	•	Net sales minus cost of goods sold and other explicitly available expenses.

Do not present gross profit as net profit.

Do not assume that Shopify sales data contains all merchant expenses.

For every calculation:
	•	Document the formula.
	•	Validate numeric inputs.
	•	Handle zero denominators.
	•	Handle negative adjustments appropriately.
	•	Handle missing values.
	•	Avoid floating-point rounding errors in monetary calculations.
	•	Use appropriate currency formatting.
	•	Keep original monetary amounts and currencies.
	•	Avoid combining different currencies without an explicit conversion source.

Display an “Estimated” label wherever the available data cannot establish an exact financial result.

Add unit tests for each calculation.

